From b4f8398478a65ef37dbb3a55a3fdd09592ecbbe0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NayiemW <37852059+NayiemW@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 02:20:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Record the genesis supply as an explicit issuance

The genesis supply is an explicit issuance record instead of a negative
issuer. Every 1/6 transfer at height 1 whose sender is the genesis
generatorPublicKey credits its recipients and does not debit the sender
(its nonce is still set). StateStore computes issued, the sum of those
items, in setGenesisBlock and returns it from getGenesisIssuance().
StateBuilder.verifyWalletsConsistency no longer exempts the genesis
sender, so no wallet may hold a negative balance. The genesis bytes do
not change.

Test: patches/tests/40-genesis-issuance.test.js (a stub devnet genesis,
and the real genesisBlock.json when $DEVNET_CRYPTO has one). The
generator ends at 0 (base: -10000000000000000) and issued is
10000000000000000.

Patch: 40
Consensus: yes
